{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq88d6gotlo","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"Workspace gremlin also bites next_action: loops aren't workspace-pinned","summary":"Finding (2026-06-10): the per-session workspace pin (mcp-core makeCall) only covers MUTATING tool calls. The loop registry stores no workspace, and next_action evaluates every loop against the daemon's GLOBAL state.workspace — when another session flipped it, our loop's heartbeat saw a 0-task graph, returned \"stop: DAG drained\", and demoted the loop mid-flight. Recovery: POST /workspace to re-pin, then loop_start with the same loopId to reactivate. Proper fix: store workspace on each loop at loop_start and evaluate that loop's decisions against ITS workspace graph, not the global pointer. Related: [[loop bootstrap race]] — second liveness bug in the same sweep/heartbeat area. Also note the 10-minute stale-claim sweep releases claims of long-running workers that don't refresh lastChanged; re-calling start_task with the same agent_id refreshes it.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-10T15:35:32.088Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq88d6gotlo","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"Workspace gremlin also bites next_action: loops aren't workspace-pinned","summary":"Finding (2026-06-10): the per-session workspace pin (mcp-core makeCall) only covers MUTATING tool calls. The loop registry stores no workspace, and next_action evaluates every loop against the daemon's GLOBAL state.workspace — when another session flipped it, our loop's heartbeat saw a 0-task graph, returned \"stop: DAG drained\", and demoted the loop mid-flight. Recovery: POST /workspace to re-pin, then loop_start with the same loopId to reactivate. Proper fix: store workspace on each loop at loop_start and evaluate that loop's decisions against ITS workspace graph, not the global pointer. Related: [[loop bootstrap race]] — second liveness bug in the same sweep/heartbeat area. Also note the 10-minute stale-claim sweep releases claims of long-running workers that don't refresh lastChanged; re-calling start_task with the same agent_id refreshes it.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-10T15:35:32.088Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:08:57.822Z"}
